# Context Indexing & Reference Routing

## Source-of-truth hierarchy (strict priority)

When a design, domain, or implementation question arises, resolve it using this cascade. Stop at the first level that answers the question.

| Priority | Source | Path | Scope |
|----------|--------|------|-------|
| 1 | Formal specification | `Doc_SMVR/SafeMining_VR_v1.1.md` | RN, RNF, HU-220–223, wireframes, traceability matrix |
| 2 | Gameplay brief | `Propuesta Simulacion LOTO.txt` | LOTO procedure steps, scenario descriptions |
| 3 | Operational knowledge base | `.agent-docs/` | Living docs: handbooks, objectives, asset lists, integration notes, QA checklists, workflows |
| 4 | Brand reference | `Doc_SMVR/paleta de colores.jpg` + `Assets/Resources/BrandConfig.asset` | Color palette, logo, visual identity |
| 5 | Cursor rules | `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` | Coding directives, architectural patterns, performance budgets |
| 6 | Cursor skills | `.cursor/skills/*/SKILL.md` | Executable procedures, subagent launch templates |
| 7 | Existing codebase | `Assets/SafeMining/` + `Assets/XR Standard Menu/` | Implementation reference, patterns to follow |
| 8 | Meta VR MCP | `meta_docs_search` / `meta_docs_get_page` | Quest SDK docs, XRI API reference |
| 9 | Ask the user | — | Last resort when all sources are exhausted |

Never assume or invent requirements. If the hierarchy is exhausted without an answer, ask the user explicitly.

## Granular document consumption protocol

`Doc_SMVR/SafeMining_VR_v1.1.md` is ~5800 lines. **Never load it fully.** Instead:

1. Open `.agent-docs/INDEX.md` — the master lookup table.
2. Find the requirement ID (RN-*, RNF-*, HU-*, module) in the index tables.
3. Read **only** the line range indicated: `Read(path, offset=<start>, limit=<span>)`.
4. Cite the ID and source file in your response before generating code or analysis.

For `.agent-docs/` files (all <100 lines), full reads are acceptable.

For `Propuesta Simulacion LOTO.txt` (100 lines), full reads are acceptable.

